#%PAM-1.0
# Tilo session-unlock PAM stack for the Tilo session installed on another
# distribution, installed as /etc/pam.d/tilo-unlock. Those hosts have no
# tilo-authd, so the lock screen checks what the host's own login checks: a
# fingerprint through fprintd where its module is installed, then the host's
# password-auth. Tilo OS ships os/etc/pam.d/tilo-unlock instead, which defers
# to its one sign-in service.
#
# Used by `tilo-unlock-helper` for the auth and account phases only.
-auth      sufficient   pam_fprintd.so
auth       substack     password-auth

account    include      password-auth
